      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225550",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/39/391592a451e201eb026c1df951319c7ba6915d9650a6b31e8d7e7ef52d932e1a.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 80$ from a population of size $N = 400$ where some individuals have a particular characteristic. Given that the proportion of those in the sample with the characteristic is $p^(^) = 0.7$, find a $90%$ confidence interval for the population proportion $p$ of individuals having this characteristic.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.645) = 0.05$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
