      ":question/problem": "![](images/db/dbf0dc13e1df28ca891afcc5f3144f9907bbaad5171f37569aff0625fd035019.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 50$ from a population of size $N = 268$ where some individuals have a particular characteristic. Given that $22%$ of the sample has the characteristic, find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population proportion $p$ of individuals having this characteristic.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 2.576) = 0.005$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\nThe required confidence interval is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
